                         loading="lazy">
                  </a>


          

      



        <div class="work-details">

<dl>
          
            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Title:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">Cracks</span> </dd>
              </div>
            
        


            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Description:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> Painting / lamp. </span> </dd>
              </div>
            




            

            

            

            

            



            

            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Size:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">20 cm x 20 cm</span> </dd>
              </div>
            

            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Medium:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value">Crackling paste on canvas, LED strip glued to a flame-retardant board and attached to back of the canvas with a velcro.</span> </dd>
              </div>
            



            

            



            

            



            

            




            
              <div class="work-detail">
                <dt> <span class="label">Date:</span> </dt>
                <dd> <span class="value"> March 2025 </span> </dd>
              </div>
            

     </dl>

    </div>]]><![CDATA[<p>More crackle paste! But now it&rsquo;s backlit. Here is what it looks like in daylight.</p>


  





























<a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/cracks/images/cracks_front_hu17454259419830643274.jpg">
    <img class="md-image"
         src="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/cracks/images/cracks_front_hu17454259419830643274.jpg"
         alt=""
         loading="lazy">
</a>


<p>The initial version consisted of the canvas and an LED strip glued to cardboard. I figured this was not the biggest brain move, so I instead got some fancy fireproof material from the local hardware store and glued the LEDs to that.</p>


  





























<a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/cracks/images/cracks_backside_hu7596951788453321165.jpg">
    <img class="md-image"
         src="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/cracks/images/cracks_backside_hu7596951788453321165.jpg"
         alt=""
         loading="lazy">
</a>


<p>I wanted to be able to remove the lights from the canvas, so I used adhesive velcro strips to attach the fancy material to the frame.</p>


  





























<a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/cracks/images/cracks_separated_hu5231253353479790833.jpg">
    <img class="md-image"
         src="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/cracks/images/cracks_separated_hu5231253353479790833.jpg"
         alt=""
         loading="lazy">
</a>


<p>I put some black insulation tape to the sides in order to block the light from coming out.</p>


  





























<a href="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/cracks/images/cracks_tape_hu13024256863539441766.jpg">
    <img class="md-image"
         src="https://tlocrt.com/visual/art/cracks/images/cracks_tape_hu13024256863539441766.jpg"
         alt=""
         loading="lazy">
</a>


]]></content:encoded></item><item><title>Colossus Rescore</title><link>https://tlocrt.com/music/colossus_rescore/</link><guid>https://tlocrt.com/music/colossus_rescore/</guid><pubDate>
